# Build output
#
# dist/ is intentionally COMMITTED. It is the compiled CLI, and shipping it is
# what makes `npx -y @vibefoundry/vibe-shield` run instantly — a registry install
# has no typescript to compile with, so without this the bin path dangles.
# Only JavaScript and declarations are tracked; source maps are excluded below.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Source maps are not needed at runtime and would triple the size of dist/.
dist/**/*.map

# Test + coverage artifacts
coverage/
.vitest-cache/

# Scanner cache
.vibe-shield-cache.json

# Generated agent artefacts (created by `vibe-shield scan --fix-prompt`)
SECURITY_PATCH_PROMPT.md

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Fixture secrets are fake and load-bearing for the test suite; they must be
# tracked or CI scans a different project than the one the developer ran.
!tests/fixtures/**/.env*

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
